'=====================================================================
' Agent name : BulkReg\02 - Build Batch
' Version    : 3.4.0  (BulkReg release; libraries BulkRegCommon + BulkRegAgents 3.4.0)
' Code       : ALL logic is in the script library BulkRegAgents (BR_RunBuildBatch).
'              This agent only calls it, so it never changes between releases.
'
' HOW TO INSTALL: open the agent, click in the editor, Ctrl+A, Delete, paste this
'              WHOLE file, Ctrl+S. Designer puts each part in its place automatically.
' Designer   : Shared agent, LotusScript
'              Runtime: On event > Action menu selection, Target: None
'              (backslash in the name = Actions > BulkReg submenu; do NOT use '|')
'
' What it does (details: BulkRegAgents > BR_RunBuildBatch):
'
' Selects the next batch of unregistered DirSync users (default 1000),
' resolves each user's home server / mail file / OU / policy / groups from
' server_mapping.csv, validates them and writes a batch file for review:
'
'   <BatchDir>\BATCH-<yyyymmdd-hhnnss>.csv          one row per user
'   <BatchDir>\BATCH-<yyyymmdd-hhnnss>_summary.txt  totals per server / policy / mail folder
'
' Mail files: name = last name (MailFileNaming), unique per home server across
' all mail folders, files on the server, Person documents and open batches;
' a clash becomes smith2.nsf, smith3.nsf (MailFileCollision=SUFFIX) or an ERROR.
' Folders mail1, mail2 ... hold at most MailFilesPerFolder (1000) mail files.
' Mail cluster (MailClusterServers): names and folders are allocated once for
' ALL cluster members, and column ClusterReplicas lists the members that will
' get a replica of the mail file (all members except the home server).
'
' Review the CSV (Excel: save as "CSV UTF-8"). You may:
'   - set Include=N to leave a user out
'   - change HomeServer, MailFile, OrgUnit, Policy, Groups, VaultServer or
'     ClusterReplicas for a user (ClusterReplicas: comma separated, empty = none)
' Rows with Check=ERROR are written with Include=N.
' Agent 03 registers ONLY rows with Include=Y from the batch file you choose.
'
' Users already listed in another OPEN batch (no _results.csv yet) are not
' selected again, so one user is never in two pending batches.
'
' Config: BatchSize (rows per batch, default 1000), BatchServerFilter (only
'         users mapped to that home server), ExtraSelection, BatchDir.
'=====================================================================
'#####################################################################
' --- part 1: (Options) ---
'#####################################################################
Option Public
Option Declare
Use "BulkRegAgents"
'#####################################################################
' --- part 2: Initialize ---
'#####################################################################
Sub Initialize
	Call BR_RunBuildBatch()
End Sub
